KNOWNBUG (unsound): [expr.prim.lambda.capture] requires a by-copy capture to be
an unnamed non-static data member of the closure object, direct-initialised
from the entity at capture time (a snapshot).  CBMC stores captures as shared
file-local symbols read at call time, so a by-copy capture behaves like a
by-reference capture and observes the post-capture value (here 20 instead of
the captured 10).  See doc/architectural/cpp-lambda-closure-support.md.
